## 2026-09-26 — SRS Revision 175: temporary Production at bodouralamal.com, sign-in not offered
- `GET /site-config` → `{ sign_in_offered }` (public, anonymous, no cookie, no personal data, `no-store`), from `SIGN_IN_OFFERED`; **absent = offered**, so every other tier is unchanged. The shared `SignInButton` renders only when offered, which hides it in the header, the mobile menu and the landing hero at once; `/login`, `/register` and the OAuth flow are untouched by Owner decision.
- Guard `check-signin-offered.sh` (proven by adding a raw OAuth link to the header → red): one control, and it asks the deployment; `/login` and `/register` are the stated exceptions. `robots.txt` allows the site, declines to advertise `/login` and `/register`.
- Verified for the privacy notice: access log carries time/request-id/method/status/bytes/timings only — **no IP, no URL, no user-agent**; the API never reads the address; `AuditLog` has no address column; a reader receives no cookie; CSP `default-src 'self'` with self-hosted fonts. **The approved IP anonymisation was unnecessary — nothing to anonymise.**
- Verification: backend typecheck/lint, OpenAPI regenerated (192 paths / 248 ops) + TD-3 conformance, frontend tsc/lint/1514 tests (5 new), doc links, `git diff --check`.
- R175 §4 host work: one certificate for `bodouralamal.com` + `www` + `staging` (issued, expires 2026-12-25); `enable-tls.sh` takes further server names for the same certificate; **the memory ceilings moved into `docker-compose.production.yml`** — they had lived only in the staging overlay, and a tier switch would have dropped them on a 4 GB host.
